          "whatsNew": {
            "en-US": "A credit card is now recognised from what its message says, not only from who sent it. The ICICI card texts from a header the app read as an ordinary bank, so on a phone where nobody had corrected it by hand the card appeared under what is left — money owed, counted as money to spend. It now reads \"Credit Card\" and the digits beside it, and files the card itself.\n\nThe digits have to sit right next to those words. A bill reminder can mention a credit card while naming the account it will be debit"
          }
        },
